From 4222051b42e73799e1d34379f7a927f3ce28ec63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JuggyMcNutty <11588877+JuggyMcNutty@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:44:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] AI level of detail: pawns out of sight think every third
 frame

FORK ONLY. This project ships a NO-AI Code Rule asking that LLM-written
changes stay in a fork and are never PR'd upstream. These were written with
Claude. Do not submit them.

Deus Ex's NPC AI is script -- ScriptedPawn's Tick event and state code, with
CheckEnemyPresence alone about a third of all script time -- and on a slow
CPU it is most of the game tick. With Settings.json
Performance.AiLevelOfDetail on (LauncherSettings), a pawn the player does not
control, that was not in view last frame and is not within ~1500 units,
skips its script Tick event and state code on two frames out of three; when
it next thinks, Tick gets all the time that passed. Movement, latent moves,
physics, animation, timers and sight checks still run every frame, so
nothing jumps, and pawns are spread over the three frames. Off by default:
a desktop has the CPU for it.

"In view" is UActor::LastVisibleFrame, set when an actor passes the
renderer's own visibility test (VisibleActor::Process), compared with
RenderSubsystem::SceneFrameStart, where the last scene's frame numbers
began. LastDrawFrame would not do: it marks every actor in a visible BSP
node, and outdoors on Liberty Island that was ~50 of 73 pawns.
